WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
20,000 optimus robots a week is Fremont's new target, turning a former car line into a robot line. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 642. SpaceX merger committees come next, then first principles on the converted plant, then cybercab sales. Fremont removed its model s and model x production line in 46 days for Optimus humanoids, ETV Barat reports. These are the first Optimus units Tesla has built to production standards. The company disclosed the start in its

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.560
its third quarter 2026 update for shareholders. Elon Musk warned that output would grow slowly

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:41.000
because Optimus is a brand new product. Tesla plans to integrate its AI-5 chip into

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:46.700
the robots by April of next year. Musk said roughly 10,000 details still need fine-tuning

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:52.440
before a million unit line reaches full capacity. Early jobs will be repetitive industrial work

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:57.904
that carries high risk. SpaceX and Tesla have each set up independent special committees

00:00:57.904 --> 00:01:03.384
to evaluate a potential merger. According to Kucoin, terms of a deal have not been set.

00:01:03.864 --> 00:01:09.764
The deal would create a company valued at approximately $3.5 trillion. That entity would own

00:01:09.764 --> 00:01:17.764
Grock, X, Starlink, TerraFab, StarMind, Robotaxi, and Optimus. A deal would need approval from 50% of

00:01:17.764 --> 00:01:23.524
Tesla shares. Musk said during SpaceX's third quarter earnings call that significant value exists

00:01:23.524 --> 00:01:26.744
in merging the companies near the superintelligence singularity.

00:01:27.224 --> 00:01:32.504
The combined entity would link rocket launches, satellite networks, custom chip manufacturing,

00:01:33.124 --> 00:01:35.444
robo-taxi services, and physical robotics.

00:01:36.542 --> 00:01:41.322
Merger committees now sit beside a cut in 2026 capital spending to $20 billion.

00:01:42.082 --> 00:01:47.222
That cut reads as an attempt to stretch existing hardware rather than fund parallel greenfield

00:01:47.222 --> 00:01:47.562
lines.

00:01:48.222 --> 00:01:52.982
Converting a vehicle line to humanoids works because both products share the same core constraints

00:01:52.982 --> 00:01:55.582
of precision motion and high-volume repetition.

00:01:56.162 --> 00:02:01.762
The robots have to meet the same repeatability standards previously demanded of vehicle bodies and battery packs.

00:02:02.182 --> 00:02:07.242
Sub-millimeter accuracy and 24-hour uptime were already bought and paid for in that building.

00:02:07.822 --> 00:02:13.162
Welding cells, vision systems, and material handling do not disappear. They get retasked.

00:02:13.542 --> 00:02:19.822
The remaining tuning is not a new category of engineering, so much as the same category is applied to a smaller, lighter payload.

00:02:19.822 --> 00:02:25.902
That payload has to operate without a driver's seat or a crash structure. The AI-5 chip is

00:02:25.902 --> 00:02:31.422
meant to deliver significantly higher onboard compute than the current AI-4 generation, with memory

00:02:31.422 --> 00:02:37.682
trim to match expected workloads. Emerged entity could route Starlink bandwidth and custom silicon directly

00:02:37.682 --> 00:02:43.102
into Optimus fleets without separate treasury functions. It cannot create additional square footage

00:02:43.102 --> 00:02:48.582
inside Fremont overnight. The weekly volume target therefore depends on yield improvements inside

00:02:48.582 --> 00:02:54.302
the repurposed space, not on construction of an entirely new factory. If those yields track the

00:02:54.302 --> 00:02:59.422
early cyber truck ramp more closely than the Model 3 ramp, external sales will arrive later

00:02:59.422 --> 00:03:04.602
than the headline schedule suggests. Every robot ship next year would carry a lower incremental

00:03:04.602 --> 00:03:10.762
capital cost than a new vehicle would have. It also carries the risk that any reliability shortfall lands

00:03:10.762 --> 00:03:17.962
on the same brand equity that supports vehicle margins. Tesla reported $1.53 billion in free cash flow

00:03:17.962 --> 00:03:21.982
for the third quarter. That came despite a 43% profit decline.

00:03:22.622 --> 00:03:26.942
The current automotive and energy businesses can still fund the transition. That holds

00:03:26.942 --> 00:03:31.242
only if the profit decline does not widen when the first customer owned Optimus units

00:03:31.242 --> 00:03:36.042
require field service. The merger committees will have to decide whether that service network

00:03:36.042 --> 00:03:41.102
is built inside Tesla's existing footprint or shared with SpaceX's orbital logistics

00:03:41.102 --> 00:03:46.782
capabilities. In both the robot and autonomy programs, the capital discipline in the spending

00:03:46.782 --> 00:03:51.742
cutting-cut forces reliance on reuse of proven manufacturing and software assets rather

00:03:51.742 --> 00:03:52.662
than fresh spending.

00:03:53.778 --> 00:03:58.338
CyberCab sales are planned to begin by the end of 2026, MotorOne reports.

00:03:58.998 --> 00:04:01.698
Early deliveries will be limited to certain ownership models.

00:04:02.258 --> 00:04:05.658
Tesla has already deployed CyberCab units into its Austin fleet.

00:04:06.158 --> 00:04:09.778
That fleet has logged nearly 2 million cumulative unsupervised miles.

00:04:10.458 --> 00:04:12.438
Mileage grew 8 times over in the quarter.

00:04:13.078 --> 00:04:15.838
Austin's service now runs from 6 in the morning to midnight.

00:04:15.838 --> 00:04:22.357
with improving weight times. Unsupervised full-self driving, or FSD, on customer-owned

00:04:22.357 --> 00:04:27.957
cars has been pushed to the second quarter of 2027. Tech Insider reports, the feature

00:04:27.957 --> 00:04:32.637
will only work inside geofence zones where Tesla already runs its Robotaxi service.

00:04:33.137 --> 00:04:38.577
That update replaces earlier promises of nationwide autonomy with a narrower fleet-managed rollout.

00:04:39.177 --> 00:04:45.157
Unsupervised capability would apply only to vehicles added to the managed Robotaxi network. Specific

00:04:45.157 --> 00:04:50.497
routes and conditions would be validated by Tesla's mapping systems. Model Y owners

00:04:50.497 --> 00:04:55.797
will be able to add their vehicles to that Robotaxi fleet through the FSD version 15 update,

00:04:56.337 --> 00:05:01.237
digital trends reports. The update enables participation in the managed network inside

00:05:01.237 --> 00:05:06.877
approved zones. Owners can interface with inbox, calendar, and tasks by voice once GROC

00:05:06.877 --> 00:05:11.860
is added to the vehicles. Tesla energy is targeting a 10 gigawatt year,

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:17.940
base and ore reports. Next year's Megapack capacity has already sold out. Utility scale

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:23.420
deployments continue to grow as a non-auto revenue engine. The backlog supports continued

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:29.494
expansion of grid software and virtual power plant offerings. A Powerwall 3 owner reported

00:05:29.494 --> 00:05:34.774
that backup power during outages still requires flipping a manual switch to activate, according

00:05:34.774 --> 00:05:40.354
to the cooldown. Commenters said the installation may not follow standard procedures for automatic

00:05:40.354 --> 00:05:46.354
transfer. Tesla has not issued a public response on whether a software or hardware fixes planned.

00:05:47.481 --> 00:05:52.841
Owners continue to compare installation practices across different storage brands. The incident leaves

00:05:52.841 --> 00:05:58.741
open questions about residential energy product reliability during real-world grid events. Apple

00:05:58.741 --> 00:06:04.681
iPad and iPhone screens now share a native Tesla app layout at the same time. I think different

00:06:04.681 --> 00:06:10.361
reports. The update improves usability across Apple device sizes without separate interfaces.

00:06:11.041 --> 00:06:16.061
Owners can manage vehicle controls, charging, and energy products from either screen format.

00:06:17.037 --> 00:06:21.417
Europe recorded a surge in monthly Tesla sales, the Wall Street Journal reports.

00:06:21.997 --> 00:06:26.957
The increase follows record deliveries in Canada, Australia, Japan, and Taiwan.

00:06:27.517 --> 00:06:33.497
The FSD supervised the tax rate grew to over 75% of new vehicle deliveries in North America.

00:06:33.497 --> 00:06:33.597
Georgia.

00:06:33.917 --> 00:06:39.219
Jean Munster said Tesla FSD is at an inflection point, according to Benzinga.

00:06:39.639 --> 00:06:41.919
He said rivals cannot match it for years.

00:06:42.639 --> 00:06:46.839
Dan Ives also highlighted that attach rate metric during commentary on the earnings.

00:06:47.976 --> 00:06:54.096
Tesla and Nvidia plan to invest $2.8 billion in Samsung Electromechanics' Binance reports.

00:06:54.656 --> 00:06:58.476
The investment targets component supply for electronics and vehicle systems.

00:06:58.476 --> 00:07:04.356
Shares of several Asian suppliers later fell after mixed third-quarter earnings and cautious outlooks.

00:07:05.192 --> 00:07:09.652
The Optimus demo will not be canned, Elon Musk said. Benzinga reports.

00:07:10.272 --> 00:07:12.712
He also said Tesla Eyes deliveries next year.

00:07:13.212 --> 00:07:17.352
He confirmed the first non-pre-programmed video is expected in one to two months.

00:07:18.012 --> 00:07:22.712
Early units will target around-the-clock industrial tasks before broader external sales.

00:07:23.766 --> 00:07:28.206
A Rivian executive urged Tesla to stop doing these calls, Yahoo Finance reports.

00:07:28.206 --> 00:07:33.366
Merger Talk reportedly created a mess for both stocks. Those comments followed

00:07:33.366 --> 00:07:37.946
pre-market slides and Tesla and SpaceX stock after the special committees were announced.

00:07:39.018 --> 00:07:43.318
Before we go, tomorrow's question is whether Tesla says anything more about when the first

00:07:43.318 --> 00:07:48.038
production standard Optimus units leave Fremont. And that's everything worth knowing about

00:07:48.038 --> 00:07:57.278
Tesla today. TSLA closed at $386.47, up $12.76, or 3.4%.

